      "writtenOn": "2021-03-24T16:03:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes. I don\u0027t like this approach but there are 55 usages of CheckSnapshot and this change covers them all.\n\nWhat I was thinking of doing was extracting the part of CheckSnapshot that runs the basic test, e.g. CheckBasicSnapshot(), and returning the FixturePreparer that can be used to create the snapshot. The CheckSnapshot method can run all the tests as it does but without the customization.\n\nAny test that needs to customize can just use CheckBasicSnapshot() and then roll their own custom test.\n\nI\u0027d rather do that as a followup and remove all this code as I have other work that would benefit from these tests.",
